{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --porcelain; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/material_engine.go | head -35; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_manifest_integrity.go | sed -n '379,398p;630,650p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage cli\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"strings\"\n     5\t\n     6\t\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n     7\t\t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/version\"\n     8\t)\n     9\t\n    10\tfunc init() {\n    11\t\tposemodel.SetEngineVersion(version.Version)\n    12\t\tposemodel.SetCurrentMaterialAt(func(root string) string {\n    13\t\t\t// A shallow checkout has no commit-bound material: it reads HEAD\n    14\t\t\t// uncached, and is unreadable (review round 1, F1).\n    15\t\t\tgit := func(limit int, args ...string) ([]byte, error) { return gitOutputBounded(root, limit, args...) }\n    16\t\t\tif shallow, err := repositoryIsShallow(git, root); err != nil || shallow {\n    17\t\t\t\treturn \"\"\n    18\t\t\t}\n    19\t\t\tout, err := gitOutputBounded(root, 1024, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"HEAD\")\n    20\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    21\t\t\t\treturn \"\"\n    22\t\t\t}\n    23\t\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n    24\t\t}, func(root, head string, in posemodel.MaterialInputs) string {\n    25\t\t\tgit := func(limit int, args ...string) ([]byte, error) { return gitOutputBounded(root, limit, args...) }\n    26\t\t\treturn materialSetDigestAt(git, root, head, in)\n    27\t\t})\n    28\t}\n   379\t\t// Only a peel that reached a commit is kept: a failed inspection or peel\n   380\t\t// may be an object not fetched yet, or a failing git, and is asked again\n   381\t\t// (review round 1, F3).\n   382\t\tpeeled := releaseTagObjects.get(filepath.Clean(root)+\"\\x00\"+object, func() (releaseTagObject, bool) {\n   383\t\t\tkind, err := gitOutput(root, \"cat-file\", \"-t\", object)\n   384\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   385\t\t\t\treturn releaseTagObject{err: fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the tag %s could not be inspected: %w\", tag, err)}, false\n   386\t\t\t}\n   387\t\t\tout, err := gitOutput(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", object+\"^{commit}\")\n   388\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   389\t\t\t\treturn releaseTagObject{err: fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrReleaseTagNotCommit, tag)}, false\n   390\t\t\t}\n   391\t\t\treturn releaseTagObject{commit: strings.TrimSpace(out), annotated: strings.TrimSpace(kind) == \"tag\"}, isGitRevision(object)\n   392\t\t})\n   393\t\treturn peeled.commit, peeled.annotated, peeled.err\n   394\t}\n   395\t\n   396\t// releaseTagRefs lists, in one git process, the object every tag's ref\n   397\t// names. ok is false when git cannot answer; the caller then reads each tag\n   398\t// on its own.\n   630\t}\n   631\t\n   632\tfunc readReleaseSnapshotAtCommit(root, tag, commit string, annotated bool) (ReleaseSnapshot, error) {\n   633\t\tkey := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s\\x00%s\\x00%s\\x00%t\", filepath.Clean(root), tag, commit, annotated)\n   634\t\tvar fresh *ReleaseSnapshot\n   635\t\tentry := releaseSnapshots.get(key, func() (releaseSnapshotEntry, bool) {\n   636\t\t\tsnap, err := readReleaseSnapshotAtCommitUncached(root, tag, commit, annotated)\n   637\t\t\tfresh = &snap\n   638\t\t\tencoded, merr := json.Marshal(snap)\n   639\t\t\t// Kept only when the read was whole: an intact snapshot, or a commit\n   640\t\t\t// that holds no manifest. A snapshot with gaps may record a failing\n   641\t\t\t// git read, and is read again (review round 1, F2).\n   642\t\t\tkeep := merr == nil && commit != \"\" && (err == nil && snap.Intact() || errors.Is(err, ErrReleaseSnapshotMissing))\n   643\t\t\treturn releaseSnapshotEntry{encoded: encoded, err: err}, keep\n   644\t\t})\n   645\t\tif fresh != nil {\n   646\t\t\treturn *fresh, entry.err\n   647\t\t}\n   648\t\tvar snap ReleaseSnapshot\n   649\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(entry.encoded, &snap); err != nil {\n   650\t\t\treturn readReleaseSnapshotAtCommitUncached(root, tag, commit, annotated)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nTwo medium blockers remain:\n\n- **N1 — successful retries are discarded**, [kept_cache.go:37](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2289309520/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go:37). After the first computation fails, waiting callers recompute outside cache coordination. Their successful results are never retained, so concurrent recovery duplicates work and later callers recompute again.\n- **N2 — eviction removes in-flight coordination**, [kept_cache.go:41](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2289309520/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go:41). Reaching capacity clears pending entries too. Another caller can then compute a key whose original computation is still running, violating R6.\n\nR1-F1 through R1-F3 are fixed. R1-F4 is partially fixed.\n\nTargeted cache tests, their race run, and shallow-checkout tests passed. Additional probes could not compile because the sandbox refused a new Go build directory; the findings above rest on source inspection. The worktree remains unchanged.\n\nRules applied: bugfix review workflow; backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Full validation conclusions below use the supplied sealed evidence. The reported performance measurement was not independently repeated.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go\",\n      \"line\": 37,\n      \"summary\": \"After an initial computation declines retention, every waiting caller invokes compute directly and discards its keep flag. If the read recovers, these callers can duplicate successful work concurrently, none publishes its success, and the next caller computes the same successful input again without any eviction. This leaves R1/R2/R3 and R6 unsatisfied. Retry through coordinated cache acquisition so a recovered success is published and shared; cover concurrent failure followed by recovery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go\",\n      \"line\": 41,\n      \"summary\": \"Capacity eviction replaces the entire entries map, including computations whose ready channels have not closed. For example, with bound 1, block computation A, request B to clear the map, then request A again: the second A computes while the original A is still running. All four production caches inherit this violation of R6 at capacity. Preserve in-flight coordination independently of retained-value eviction and cover a capacity crossing while a key is pending.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/material_engine.go:16 checks shallow eligibility on each graph HEAD resolution; material_binding.go rejects empty and unreadable digests from retention. Targeted current-material tests passed, as did go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestChangeSetMaterialDigestIsUnreadableInAShallowCheckout|TestShallowAnswerFollowsTheCheckout' -count=1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_manifest_integrity.go:642 retains only intact snapshots or proven manifest absence. Git read failures represented by gaps fail Intact(). TestASnapshotWithGapsIsReadAgain and TestAFailedReleaseSnapshotReadIsNotKept passed in the targeted test run and race run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/release_manifest_integrity.go:383-391 declines retention after either inspection or commit-peel failure. TestAFailedReleaseTagPeelIsAskedAgain passed in the targeted test run and race run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R1-F4\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All four caches now use keptCache; successful concurrent misses wait on ready and TestAKeptValueIsComputedOnceForConcurrentMisses passed, including under -race. However, kept_cache.go:37 bypasses coordination after a declined computation and :41 drops pending entries at capacity. Remaining cases are N1 and N2.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the sealed bf2ff02c31752a3343b0200fa62b27c220ce2453..597cbd9a8ad1a668d04fb5196707ca195c2da84c implementation and governance changes against spec R1-R6 and D1. Swept all four cache keys, shared-value mutation, failed-read retention and recovery, concurrent misses, bounds and eviction, shallow-state eligibility, moved HEAD and tag refs, listed-versus-individual tag resolution, snapshot copies, bundle loss attribution, production call sites, regression tests, and validation-matrix registration. Consulted applicable rules and relevant cache/runtime knowledge. Ran targeted cache tests, targeted race tests, shallow-checkout tests, artifact-check, surface-check, suggest-review, recurrence-check, and diff whitespace checks. Repository status remained clean. Additional in-memory-overlay probes were blocked before compilation by the read-only Go temporary directory; they are not claimed as executed evidence.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined content-addressed keys, fresh ref resolution, shallow eligibility, copy ownership, and retry assumptions. Verified ordinary reuse and failure rejection with code and targeted tests. The harne8 timing and byte equality remain implementer measurements, not independently repeated facts. Remaining coordination assumptions are explicitly rejected in N1 and N2; the spec's separate check-performance follow-up remains outside this scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected unchanged public CLI, MCP, and persisted schemas. Cache changes remain internal; returned snapshot data is copied and error contracts are preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Invalid tags, missing manifests, unreadable material, snapshot gaps, and failed peels remain rejected or retryable. Targeted negative tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected CLI hook registration, graph material recomputation, archive loading, release snapshot consumers, and review-header consumers. Production composition remains connected.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected retained error context and source-loss attribution. Git failures and snapshot gaps remain diagnosable, and cached bundle losses receive the current file's artifact path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared changed readers and their callers. No public schema or comma